<% layout('/layouts/boilerplate') -%>
<div class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-8">
  <h1 class="mb-3">About SPACER</h1>
  <p class="lead">SPACER stands for <strong>Vehicle Accommodation Zone</strong>. It is a parking marketplace where drivers book a bay in advance and owners list space that would otherwise sit empty.</p>
  <h4 class="mt-4">The problem</h4>
  <p>Searching for parking wastes time and fuel, and unused private parking earns nothing. SPACER connects the two sides and removes the guesswork.</p>
  <h4 class="mt-4">Smart pricing and demand forecast</h4>
  <p>Each hour's price is the owner's base rate multiplied by three factors: time of day, expected demand, and how full the zone already is. The total always stays between 0.8x and 2.0x of the base rate, and the booking page shows the breakdown. Owners get a forecast built from past bookings, compared against a simple "same hour yesterday" baseline, plus plain-language price suggestions.</p>
  <div class="alert alert-info">Figures from the demo data and simulation are <strong>simulated</strong>. They show how the method behaves and are indicative, not field-measured.</div>
</div></div>
